lpeg 1.1.0: initialize CapState.firstcap in the match-time (Cmt) path

`runtimecap` is called from the VM's ICloseRunTime handler with a fresh
CapState whose `firstcap` is never initialized — it is only assigned in
`getcaptures` (the match-end path).  An accumulator capture (`patt % f`)
nested inside a `lpeg.Cmt` group then reads stack garbage in
`accumulatorcap` ("no previous value for accumulator capture" or silent
misbehaviour), depending on the build's stack layout.  Set it to the
slot where the first nested captured value will go, matching the
`getcaptures` convention.

Upstream bug — drop this patch once an lpeg release ships the fix.
--- a/lpcap.c
+++ b/lpcap.c
@@ -342,6 +342,7 @@
   pushluaval(cs);  /* push function to be called */
   lua_pushvalue(L, SUBJIDX);  /* push original subject */
   lua_pushinteger(L, s - cs->s + 1);  /* push current position */
+  cs->firstcap = lua_gettop(L) + 1;  /* where first nested value goes */
   n = pushnestedvalues(cs, 0);  /* push nested captures */
   lua_call(L, n + 2, LUA_MULTRET);  /* call dynamic function */
   if (id > 0) {  /* are there old dynamic captures to be removed? */
